      "summary": "TSMC files application for proposed 2nm chip fab in Brazos County, Texas Data Center Dynamics",
      "body": "TSMC has submitted an application outlining its proposal to build at least one 2nm chip fab on a 3,232-acre parcel of land in Brazos County, Texas.\nThe chipmaker filed the application with the State Comptroller’s office on November 23.\nThe land sits to the north of Knope Bridge Road and west of I&GN Road. Brazos County is home to the main campus of Texas A&M University and is located around 100 miles (161 kms) northwest of Houston and 100 miles east of Austin.\nHowever, local news outlet KBTX reported that despite government officials stating the sites were under contract, county records show that TSMC has not yet purchased the land. The application states that while the chipmaker has “authorized agents to enter into non-binding agreements relating to potential land acquisitions… these agreements in no way commit the company to acquire land or make a final site selection decision.”\nOfficials additionally told KBTX that TSMC was still evaluating other sites for its proposed Texas fab, in",
