      "source": "SemiEngineering",
      "url": "https://semiengineering.com/securing-the-chiplet-future-with-a-ucie-4-0-aware-verification-architecture/",
      "summary": "Bringing together compliance tests, protocol-aware monitoring, transaction recording, scoreboarding, error-injection callbacks, and targeted debug to support multiple layers. The post Securing The Chiplet Future With A UCIe 4.0-Aware Verification Architecture appeared first on Semiconductor Engineering.",
      "body": "Verifying the new features and options in UCIe 4.0 requires evidence that state transitions are correct, errors detected and corrected, and recovery preserves the behavior required by the design. Siemens Avery UCIe VIP brings together compliance tests, protocol-aware monitoring, transaction recording, scoreboarding, error-injection callbacks, and targeted debug to support this work across multiple layers. Used with a verification plan derived from the exact UCIe revision and the design’s supported options, these capabilities help teams build a connected view of both normal operation and failure response.\n\nRead more here.\n\nFig.1: Siemens Avery UCIe VIP – Verification Architecture\n\nThe post Securing The Chiplet Future With A UCIe 4.0-Aware Verification Architecture appeared first on Semiconductor Engineering.",
