      "summary": "Validate UCIe.mem implementations across development stages while reusing a common verification environment. The post Verifying UCIe.mem: Flexible Verification For Compute And Memory Chiplets appeared first on Semiconductor Engineering.",
      "body": "By Ujjwal Negi and Prashant Dixit\n\nAs chiplet-based designs become increasingly common, connecting compute and memory dies efficiently is an important part of building scalable systems. The Universal Chiplet Interconnect Express (UCIe) standard provides a common die-to-die interconnect, while UCIe.mem defines a standardized protocol for memory transactions between compute and memory chiplets.\n\nWhy UCIe.mem matters\n\nModern systems can combine compute chiplets with different memory technologies, including HBM, DDR, and LPDDR. Traditionally, integrating these components can involve technology-specific interfaces and custom mechanisms. UCIe.mem addresses the growing need for scalable and flexible memory architectures in modern computing systems by providing a common, memory-technology-agnostic way to communicate memory requests and responses across chiplets.\n\nThis standardization provides a foundation for more modular and scalable chiplet-based architectures. It allows compute and memory c",
